⚡🇺🇸🇮🇶 TLDR on the Iraqi Prime Ministers visit to Washington and his meeting with Trump;

United States President Donald Trump and Iraqi Prime Minister Ali al-Zaidi have met at the White House in Washington, DC, with both leaders pledging to deepen economic ties and boost Iraq’s oil output.

During their Oval Office meeting, President Trump praised a "tremendous chemistry" with al-Zaidi, highlighting their shared backgrounds as wealthy businessmen who entered politics from the private sector. Media outlets like The Washington Post noted a lighter moment when Trump congratulated al-Zaidi on a "conclusive election victory," though al-Zaidi was actually appointed as a consensus compromise candidate rather than being directly on an election ballot.

They both pledged to transition their bilateral relationship from a militaristic/security focus to an economic partnership. The delegation is expected to sign multiple memorandums of understanding to bring U.S. companies into Iraq's oil and gas sectors.

This is also not to mention, the United States is putting significan pressure on Iraq to rein in and or disarm Iran backed militias within Iraq, a pressure that was most certainly applied on Al Zaidi, and other Iraqi politicians have echoed the same call.

